flowchart TD
    Start([Executor::step_uop]) --> Halt{Halted?}
    Halt -->|yes| End([Return])
    Halt -->|no| State{Execution state}
    State -->|FETCH| Fetch[Read first unit at PC with execute access; decode opcode and fetch remaining units]
    Fetch --> DecodeNext[Set state to DECODE] --> End
    State -->|DECODE| Decode[Decode instruction; reject invalid encoding or register index]
    Decode --> ExecuteNext[Reset execution counters; set state to EXECUTE_UOPS] --> End
    State -->|EXECUTE_UOPS| Mode{Latency mode}
    Mode -->|dynamic| Dynamic[Execute sequentially; ALU operations can take multiple cycles]
    Mode -->|bottleneck| Bottleneck[Execute sequentially and wait until instruction latency is met]
    Mode -->|additive| Additive[Execute sequentially then wait instruction latency cycles]
    Mode -->|strict| Strict[Spread or batch micro-ops across target cycles]
    Dynamic & Bottleneck & Additive & Strict --> Finished{Execution complete?}
    Finished -->|no| End
    Finished -->|yes| DoneNext[Set state to DONE] --> End
    State -->|DONE| PC{PC unchanged and not explicitly modified?}
    PC -->|yes| Advance[Advance PC by fetched units in bytes]
    PC -->|no| Interrupt
    Advance --> Interrupt{Interrupt pending?}
    Interrupt -->|yes| Save[If SP exists, push next PC; set PC to interrupt ID]
    Interrupt -->|no| Reset
    Save --> Reset[Clear PC modification flag; set state to FETCH] --> End
